Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-02
Subject: Use runtime SizeOf for pointer-width conditionals
License: expat

FPC 2.6.0 uses {$if sizeof(...)} in compiler implementation code to choose between 32-bit and 64-bit pointer-sized paths.  That requires the bootstrap translator preprocessor to resolve Pascal type sizes while scanning conditional directives.

Use normal Pascal SizeOf checks instead.  The affected sites are executable code, so both branches can remain visible to the parser and the compiler can choose the same path at run time without requiring type-aware preprocessor evaluation.

--- a/compiler/defutil.pas
+++ b/compiler/defutil.pas
@@ -988,13 +988,14 @@
           procvardef:
             begin
               if not tprocvardef(def).is_addressonly then
-                {$if sizeof(pint) = 4}
-                  result:=OS_64
-                {$else} {$if sizeof(pint) = 8}
-                  result:=OS_128
-                {$else}
-                  internalerror(200707141)
-                {$endif} {$endif}
+                begin
+                  if sizeof(pint) = 4 then
+                    result:=OS_64
+                  else if sizeof(pint) = 8 then
+                    result:=OS_128
+                  else
+                    internalerror(200707141);
+                end
               else
                 result:=OS_ADDR;
             end;
